.TH "atexit_do" "3" "2026\-10\-03" "TheCRatTime" "AtExit reference"
.SH NAME
\fBatexit\fR \- forget about the forgotten \fBfree\fR(3)
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is small library, that only does one thing: call functions at exit.\&
.PP
See \fBREADME.md\fR in project or if you installed and built project, you can see man-pages about functions.\&
.PP
.SS List of functions
\fBInitAtExit\fR(3)
.RS 4
Init \fBAtExitHeader\fR struct.\&
.RE
.PP
\fBSetAtExit\fR(3)
.RS 4
Set function, that will be called at \fBDoAtExit\fR(3).\&
.RE
.PP
\fBAtExitClean\fR(3)
.RS 4
Clean all \fBAtExitHeader\fR without running \fBDoAtExit\fR(3).\&
.RE
.PP
\fBDoAtExit\fR(3)
.RS 4
Run all \fBAtExitHeader\fR struct.\&
.RE
.PP
\fBAtExitMalloc\fR(3)
.RS 4
This is wrapper for \fBmalloc\fR(3), doing \fBmalloc\fR(3) and set to \fBAtExitHeader\fR function \fBfree\fR(3).\&
.RE
.PP
\fBAtExitFopen\fR(3)
.RS 4
Also wrapper, but for \fBfopen\fR(3), doing \fBfopen\fR(3) and set to \fBAtExitHeader\fR function \fBfclose\fR(3).\&
.RE
.PP
\fBatexit_defer\fR(3)
.RS 4
Macro, that equals \fBSetAtExit\fR.\& Just write \fBdefer\fR.\& Needed write \fB#define USE_DEFER\fR.\&
.RE
.PP
\fBAtExitFree\fR(3),
.RS 4
Free \fBAtExitHeader\fR struct with function \fBfree\fR(3).\&
.RE
.PP
.SH AUTHORS
Project and man-page: TheCRatTime
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
